QUESTION: a. Write a program to implement numpy and pandas packages. 

ALGORITHM:

1.Start
2.Import NumPy and Pandas libraries
3.Create a NumPy array
4.Perform operations like sum, mean, max, and min
5.Reshape the array and perform matrix operations
6.Create a dictionary dataset
7.Convert dictionary into Pandas DataFrame
8.Access columns and display summary
9.Add a new column
10.Filter and sort the data
11.Display results
12.Stop

CODE:
import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

print("----- NUMPY OPERATIONS -----")

arr = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])
print("Array:", arr)

print("Sum:", np.sum(arr))
print("Mean:", np.mean(arr))
print("Max:", np.max(arr))
print("Min:", np.min(arr))

arr2 = arr.reshape(5, 1)
print("Reshaped Array:\n", arr2)

matrix = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
print("Matrix:\n", matrix)

print("Transpose:\n", matrix.T)
print("Matrix Multiplication:\n", np.dot(matrix, matrix))


print("\n----- PANDAS OPERATIONS -----")

data = {
    "Name": ["Yukthi", "Manish", "Siya"],
    "Marks": [85, 90, 88],
    "City": ["Chennai", "Delhi", "Mumbai"]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)
print("DataFrame:\n", df)

print("\nNames:\n", df["Name"])

print("\nSummary:\n", df.describe())

df["Grade"] = ["A", "A+", "A"]
print("\nAfter Adding Column:\n", df)

print("\nStudents with Marks > 85:\n", df[df["Marks"] > 85])

print("\nSorted by Marks:\n", df.sort_values(by="Marks"))
